<%# One account row. Local: row (Subscriptions::AccountSummaries::Row).

    SHARED by the cockpit block (K1) and the account index (K2) on purpose: both answer
    "which accounts are mine and what do they cost", and two copies of that answer would
    be two places for the money wording to drift apart.

    The seat count is always shown, the AMOUNT only when the account is actually billed
    (Row#amount_shown?). With billing_starts_on NULL nobody has decided whether this
    account is invoiced at all (E4), and a euro figure there reads as an invoice no one
    promised. That is today's normal state, not an edge case: it holds for every account
    on production.

    policy(...).manage_billing? is `owner?`, a plain id comparison and NOT a query, so
    asking it per row costs nothing. It gates the completeness hint because E6 makes the
    billing master data owner-only, and "yours are incomplete" is a statement about them. %>
<%= link_to billing_account_path(row.account),
            class: 'flex items-center justify-between gap-4 p-4 border-b border-cream-200 last:border-b-0 hover:bg-cream-100 transition-colors' do %>
  <div class="min-w-0">
    <div class="font-bold text-sm text-cream-900 truncate"><%= row.account.name %></div>
    <div class="text-xs text-cream-500 truncate mt-0.5">
      <%= row.organisations.map(&:name).join(', ') %>
    </div>
    <% if policy(row.account).manage_billing? && !row.account.billing_complete? %>
      <div class="text-xs font-bold text-amber-700 mt-1">
        <%= t('views.billing_accounts.row.incomplete') %>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <div class="text-right flex-shrink-0">
    <% if row.amount_shown? %>
      <div class="font-mono text-sm font-bold text-cream-900">
        <%= format_price_cents(row.amount.total_cents, row.amount.currency) %>
      </div>
    <% else %>
      <%# Dynamic key, pinned for every state by spec/locales/billing_account_row_states_spec.rb
          in BOTH locales: raise_on_missing_translations is off in the test environment and
          i18n-tasks does not see a reference without a definition, so a fifth state would
          otherwise render "translation missing" into the customer page without failing. %>
      <div class="text-xs text-cream-600 max-w-[16rem]">
        <%= t("views.billing_accounts.row.state.#{row.state}") %>
      </div>
    <% end %>
    <div class="text-xs text-cream-500 mt-0.5">
      <%= t('views.billing_accounts.row.seats', count: row.seats) %>
    </div>
  </div>
<% end %>
